Subject: [PATCH] Bound Matroska longjmp recovery to live parser state

Local patch against the upstream v3.5.0 release; not submitted upstream.
The current upstream parser is identical to the release parser.

Keep only reindex's mutable scan cursor and failed-attempt counter volatile,
with a single checkpoint around the scan. Other attempt-local values are
reassigned before use after recovery. Restore the caller's handler before
fallback cue allocation, so allocation failure cannot re-enter a completed
scan. Preserve the 50-failure skip and block reader's three-retry limit.

nSeekHeads is never used after recovery, so restrict its scope to the parsing
branch. The block reader's result is also reassigned after recovery: put the
parsing attempt in a helper without setjmp instead of making its locals
volatile. These lifetimes follow C 7.13.2.1's rules for automatic objects.

Add synthetic malformed/truncated EBML, retry/progress, SeekHead-cycle and
allocation-failure regression tests. The unpatched parser fails the fallback
allocation test by rescanning the same position.

